{"ref":"BDB, תְּעָלָה","hw":"תְּעָלָה","html":"† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">תְּעָלָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. water-course</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">ת׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 30:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.30.13\">Je 30:13</a> +; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּעָלַת</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:3\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.3\">Is 7:3</a> + 2 times; pl. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּעָלֹתֶיהָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 31:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.31.4\">Ez 31:4</a>;—<br><strong>a.</strong>  <em>water-course</em>, conducted for irrigation <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 31:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.31.4\">Ez 31:4</a>; hence poet., channel for rain <a data-ref=\"Job 38:25\" href=\"/Job.38.25\">Jb 38:25</a>.<br><strong>b.</strong>  <em>conduit</em>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 18:17\" href=\"/II_Kings.18.17\">2 K 18:17</a> = <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 36:2\" href=\"/Isaiah.36.2\">Is 36:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:3\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.3\">Is 7:3</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"II Kings 20:20\" href=\"/II_Kings.20.20\">2 K 20:20</a>.<br><strong>c.</strong>  <em>trench</em>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:32\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.32\">1 K 18:32</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:35\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.35\">35</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:38\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.38\">38</a>.","next":"BDB, תְּעָלָה²","prev":"BDB, מַעֲלָה²"}